#---
# purpose: "Two hundred closures that allocate when called share one body frame of two slots a closure"
# oracle: self
# oracle.stamp: 167e078114f4e54e
#---
#
# `main` holds two hundred closures, each capturing one integer, and then
# calls every one. The calls cut the body into a continuation per call, and
# the continuations run in one frame that holds each live value once: the
# frame's slot count grows with the closures, not with their square. Each
# closure allocates when it is called, so collections run while the frame is
# live and read the slot count its header states.
defmodule Main do
  def main() do
    k0 = 0
    c0 = fn x -> length(Enum.map(Enum.to_list(1..3000), fn v -> {v, v} end)) - 3000 + x + k0 end
    k1 = 1
    c1 = fn x -> length(Enum.map(Enum.to_list(1..3000), fn v -> {v, v} end)) - 3000 + x + k1 end
    k2 = 2
